  "question": "If force ($F$), length ($L$) and time ($T$) are taken as fundamental quantities, the dimensional formula of mass is",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$[FLT^{-2}]$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$[FL^{-1}T^{2}]$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$[FL^{-1}T^{-2}]$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$[FL^{2}T^{-2}]$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "From $F = ma$, we get $m = \\dfrac{F}{a}$. Acceleration has dimensions $[LT^{-2}]$, so\n$$[m] = \\frac{[F]}{[LT^{-2}]} = [FL^{-1}T^{2}]$$",
